  "worked_solution": "The total number of the characters is $5$, so there are $5!$ ways of arranging them:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5! & =5\\times 4\\times 3\\times 2\\times 1 \\\\  & =120.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe code \"$yz246$\" is one of them. By subtracting $1$ from $120,$ we find the number of the different codes that can be formed beside \"$yz246$\".\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}120-1=119\\end{aligned}\n$$",
